  "worked_solution": "The Newton-Raphson process for optimization is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}{{f}^{″}({x}_{n})},\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ and ${f}^{″}({x}_{n})$ are the first and second derivatives of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n},$ respectively.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{6}-2{x}^{5}+{x}^{2})^{′}=6{x}^{5}-10{x}^{4}+2x, \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =(6{x}^{5}-10{x}^{4}+2x)^{′}=30{x}^{4}-40{x}^{3}+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{6{x}_{n}^{5}-10{x}_{n}^{4}+2{x}_{n}}{30{x}_{n}^{4}-40{x}_{n}^{3}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}(30{x}_{n}^{4}-40{x}_{n}^{3}+2)-(6{x}_{n}^{5}-10{x}_{n}^{4}+2{x}_{n})}{30{x}_{n}^{4}-40{x}_{n}^{3}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{24{x}_{n}^{5}-30{x}_{n}^{4}}{30{x}_{n}^{4}-40{x}_{n}^{3}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12{x}_{n}^{5}-15{x}_{n}^{4}}{15{x}_{n}^{4}-20{x}_{n}^{3}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=1.8,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{12{x}_{0}^{5}-15{x}_{0}^{4}}{15{x}_{0}^{4}-20{x}_{0}^{3}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{12(1.8)^{5}-15(1.8)^{4}}{15(1.8)^{4}-20(1.8)^{3}+1} \\\\  & =1.656\\,564….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{12{x}_{1}^{5}-15{x}_{1}^{4}}{15{x}_{1}^{4}-20{x}_{1}^{3}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{12(1.656\\,564…)^{5}-15(1.656\\,564…)^{4}}{15(1.656\\,564…)^{4}-20(1.656\\,564…)^{3}+1} \\\\  & =1.594\\,573…, \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{12{x}_{2}^{5}-15{x}_{2}^{4}}{15{x}_{2}^{4}-20{x}_{2}^{3}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{12(1.594\\,573…)^{5}-15(1.594\\,573…)^{4}}{15(1.594\\,573…)^{4}-20(1.594\\,573…)^{3}+1} \\\\  & =1.582\\,950…, \\\\ {x}_{4} & =\\frac{12{x}_{3}^{5}-15{x}_{3}^{4}}{15{x}_{3}^{4}-20{x}_{3}^{3}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{12(1.582\\,950…)^{5}-15(1.582\\,950…)^{4}}{15(1.582\\,950…)^{4}-20(1.582\\,950…)^{3}+1} \\\\  & =1.582\\,567….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the last two approximations ${x}_{3}≈1.58$ and ${x}_{4}≈1.58$ are the same when rounded to two decimal places.\n\nTherefore, the critical point of the function is $x≈1.58,$ rounded to two decimal places.",
